{"Title":"Order relative to authorizing the joint committee on Education to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents relative to education matters.","BillNumber":"S2616","DocketNumber":null,"GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"J14","Name":"Joint Committee on Education","Type":2,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14","ResponseDate":"2024-01-31T11:24:09.6"},"Cosponsors":[],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S2616/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Order","Pinslip":"Senate, February 8, 2024 -- The committee on Education, to whom was referred the petitions (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 258) of Julian Cyr for legislation relative to the availability of sunscreen for students; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 281) of Barry R. Finegold for legislation relative to school improvements in the town of Wilmington; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 298) of Edward J. Kennedy, Vanna Howard, Rady Mom, Rodney M. Elliott and other members of the General Court for legislation relative to increased material costs in school construction projects; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 303) of Jason M. Lewis and Rebecca L. Rausch for legislation to increase the Commonwealth's share of the education foundation budget; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 316) of Paul W. Mark for legislation relative to best management practices for wireless in schools and public institutions of higher education; (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 319) of Liz Miranda and Lydia Edwards for legislation relative to create a commercial driver’s license pilot program at Madison Park technical vocational high school; and (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 360) of John C. Velis, Danillo A. Sena and Ryan C. Fattman for legislation to establish an elementary and secondary school robotics grant program, report the accompanying Order  (Senate, No. 2616).","DocumentText":"\tOrdered, That the committee on Education be authorized and directed to make an investigation and study of certain current Senate documents numbered 258, 281, 298, 303, 316, 319, and 360 relative to education matters.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Study","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]},{"Action":"Discharge to Another Committee","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J40","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J40"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}